==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|sunnentac|sunne(n)tac}}, {{m|gmh|sunntac|sun(n)tac}}, from {{inh|de|goh|sunnūntag}} (9th c.), from late {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*sunnōn dag||day of the sun}}, a calque of {{der|de|la|diēs Sōlis}} (4th c.). Compare {{cog|nds|Sünndag}}, {{cog|nl|zondag}}, {{cog|fy|snein}}, {{cog|en|Sunday}}, {{cog|da|søndag}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈzɔntaːk/|[ˈzɔntʰaˑkʰ]}} {{a|standard}}
* {{audio|de|De-Sonntag.ogg|audio}}
:* {{IPA|de|/ˈzɔntax/}} {{a|northern Germany and parts of central Germany; chiefly colloquial}}
:* {{IPA|de|/ˈzɔntaːx/}} {{a|parts of central Germany; chiefly colloquial}}
* {{rhymes|de|aːɡ̊}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|Sonntages|gen2=Sonntags|Sonntage}}

# [[Sunday]] (the first day of the week in many religious traditions, and the seventh day of the week in systems using the [[w:ISO 8601|ISO 8601]] standard)

